{"nodes": [{"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_uzcasting_backend_architecture", "label": "UzCasting Backend Architecture", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spring Boot 3.1.2 / Java 17 / Maven / PostgreSQL layered monolith; the frontend build is packed into the fat jar so one artifact serves the whole site. Must be started from the repo root because Attachment writes to the relative path backend/files/."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_layered_monolith", "label": "Layered Monolith (Controller-Service-Repository)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71, \u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capitalised package names are non-standard but consistent, so they are kept; new PHASE 3+ modules follow the same convention."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_jwt_authentication", "label": "JWT Authentication (typed access/refresh tokens)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A typ claim separates access from refresh because previously both were identical and a stolen refresh token opened the entire API; access life was cut from 100 to 15 minutes."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_refresh_token_rotation", "label": "Refresh Token Rotation and Revocation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "refresh_token table (V25) stores only the jti, never the token text; each refresh revokes the previous one and a replayed revoked token is treated as theft, closing the user's whole chain. Delivered as an httpOnly+Secure+SameSite=Strict cookie, never in the response body."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_loginattemptservice", "label": "LoginAttemptService (per-account lockout)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five failures lock an account for 15 minutes; IP-level throttling is a separate RateLimitFilter so the two cannot mask each other."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_googletokenverifier", "label": "GoogleTokenVerifier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_platformrole_hierarchy", "label": "PlatformRole Hierarchy (HYPER_ADMIN to USER)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Higher roles inherit lower rights; WORKER is governed by fine-grained Permissions; staff creation is checked at the endpoint so privilege escalation is impossible. Hiding a frontend menu is not security - every endpoint checks independently. The legacy UserRoles enum is preserved (production rows exist) and mapped via RoleMapper."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_storageservice", "label": "StorageService Abstraction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Local/Timeweb/S3 implementations behind one interface so the provider name never leaks into business logic; uploads stream via Files.copy so large video never loads fully into RAM. Extension allowlist, fully server-side file names, and normalize()+startsWith(ROOT) checks on both write and read."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_mediaasset", "label": "MediaAsset Entity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "New entity added instead of touching the legacy Attachment, which is still live in the Telegram bot flow."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_cms_content_model", "label": "CMS Content Model (Content/Season/Episode/EpisodeVideo)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lives in a separate Cms.* package so it never mixes with the legacy Entity/Repository (D16), and must be listed in @EntityScan/@EnableJpaRepositories or the repositories are not found. There is deliberately no single episode.videoUrl field - an EpisodeVideo list supports multiple parts and dubbing languages. @Version detects two admins editing at once, deletedAt gives soft delete, prices are BigDecimal, list queries use @EntityGraph against N+1."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_translation_tables", "label": "Separate Translation Tables (not JSON columns)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Text goes into per-parent tables with UNIQUE(parent_id, locale) rather than a JSON column because search and indexing must work per language. Media locale is optional: NULL means all languages, an explicit locale wins when present, so a per-language poster is possible but not mandatory."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_accesspolicy", "label": "AccessPolicy (FREE/PREMIUM_ONLY/PURCHASE_ONLY/PREMIUM_OR_PURCHASE)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Entitlement can arrive from four sources - single episode purchase (default 3000 sum stored in the DB, not hardcoded), whole-premiere purchase, an active Premium subscription, or free content. Casting projects are covered by Premium but never by one-off purchase."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_accessservice_canwatch", "label": "AccessService.canWatch (single access gate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One entry point so the rule is never scattered across the client or several services; the lock in the episode list and the lock on the watch page derive from the same call and therefore cannot drift apart."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_userbalance", "label": "UserBalance (money, Stars, Coins)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exchange rates and packages are admin-managed settings rather than code constants."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_donationtransaction", "label": "DonationTransaction (immutable)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No hard delete; donations are accounted separately per content and per creator."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_analytics_model", "label": "Two-Layer Analytics Model (raw events to daily aggregates)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The dashboard never runs COUNT(*) over millions of raw events; when there is no data it shows an empty state rather than a fabricated number."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_auditlog", "label": "AuditLog", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Records actor, action, entity, before/after, ip and user agent; passwords, tokens and payment credentials are never written, and a plain Admin cannot delete audit rows."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_flyway_migrations", "label": "Flyway Migration Plan (baseline-on-migrate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "V1__baseline.sql records the existing schema; ddl-auto only moves from update to validate after the baseline is verified in production."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_timezone_config", "label": "Asia/Tashkent Timezone Setting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Over 310 LocalDateTime uses carry no zone, so without app.timezone the container's UTC made a scheduled premiere publish five hours late."}, {"id": "roadmap_backend_architecture_id_strategy", "label": "Per-Entity ID Strategy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Existing entities keep their id types (User UUID, CastingUser Integer, Role manual int as technical debt) because production rows exist; all new entities use Long + IDENTITY."}], "edges": [{"source": "roadmap_backend_architecture_uzcasting_backend_architecture", "target": "roadmap_backend_roadmap_backend_checklist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "header 'Task ro'yxati \u2192 BACKEND_ROADMAP.md'", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_backend_architecture_jwt_authentication", "target": "roadmap_my_idea_authentication", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 '(\u00a761)'", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_backend_architecture_refresh_token_rotation", "target": "roadmap_my_idea_authentication", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 refresh_token V25 (\u00a761)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_backend_architecture_jwt_authentication", "target": "roadmap_backend_architecture_refresh_token_rotation", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 typ claim / jti", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_backend_architecture_timezone_config", "target": "roadmap_my_idea_time_rule", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 '(\u00a768)'", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_backend_architecture_platformrole_hierarchy", "target": "roadmap_my_idea_role_hierarchy", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "roadmap/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_backend_architecture_platformrole_hierarchy", "target": "roadmap_my_idea_backend_authorization", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, 